# A host that is down, gone or limits its clients, and where the same Git
# repositories or files are (arch/import.py tries it after the host itself).
# A prefix may be a whole URL. A file from here is checked as the URL's: the
# PKGBUILD's checksums, or arch/resum's for a file served changed.
https://dev.gnupg.org/source/	https://github.com/gpg/
# docbook.org's files moved to its archive (BLFS gives the same MD5 for both)
https://www.docbook.org/	https://archive.docbook.org/
# newt left pagure.io for GitLab (the same tags; GitLab's archive is
# git archive | gzip -n of the tag)
https://pagure.io/newt/archive/	https://gitlab.com/newt-ui/newt/-/archive/
# Savannah's cgit times out; GitHub's mirror has the commit (the same diff)
https://cgit.git.savannah.gnu.org/cgit/autoconf-archive.git/patch/?id=241f7ae5f857b0c9bab7866b79b4e47587126b96	https://github.com/autoconf-archive/autoconf-archive/commit/241f7ae5f857b0c9bab7866b79b4e47587126b96.patch
# NSS's Mercurial repository (hg.mozilla.org) has a Git mirror with the
# same tags (NSS_3_134_RTM...): cloned as the PKGBUILD's nss directory
hg+https://hg.mozilla.org/projects/nss	git+https://github.com/nss-dev/nss
# without www. too (docbook5-xml's)
https://docbook.org/	https://archive.docbook.org/
# Savannah's Git times out from the runners: gnulib (wget's source and
# submodule) is mirrored on GitHub
https://git.savannah.gnu.org/git/gnulib.git	https://github.com/coreutils/gnulib.git
# ftp.gnu.org times out from the runners: kernel.org's GNU mirror (the same
# files, checked against the PKGBUILD's sums)
https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/	https://mirrors.kernel.org/gnu/
# download.drobilla.net times out: Debian's copy of the release (its
# orig.tar.xz is upstream's file; the PKGBUILD's sums check it)
https://download.drobilla.net/zix-0.8.2.tar.xz	https://deb.debian.org/debian/pool/main/z/zix/zix_0.8.2.orig.tar.xz
